@page 52 morning-prayer
c __MORNING PRAYER.__
P Thou art the King of Glory: O Christ;
P Thou art the everlasting Son: of the Father.
P When thou tookest upon thee to deliver
  man: thou didst not abhor the Virgin’s womb.
P When thou hadst overcome the sharpness
  of death: thou didst open the Kingdom of
  Heaven to all believers.
P Thou sittest at the right hand of God: in
  the glory of the Father.
P We believe that thou shalt come: to be our
  Judge.
P We therefore pray thee, help thy servants:
  whom thou hast redeemed with thy precious
  blood.
P Make them to be numbered with thy saints:
  in glory everlasting.
P O Lord, save thy people: and bless thine
  heritage.
P Govern them: and lift them up for ever.
P Day by day: we magnify thee;
P And we worship thy Name: ever, world with-
  out end.
P Vouchsafe, O Lord: to keep us this day
  without sin.
P O Lord, have mercy upon us: have mercy
  upon us.
P O Lord, let thy mercy lighten upon us: as
  our trust is in thee.
P O Lord, in thee have I trusted: let me ne-
  ver be confounded.
f ¶ __Or__
